    {
      "id": "l01",
      "start": 0.45,
      "end": 4.543,
      "text": "Sunglasses on, and your phone goes black. Turn it, and it's back. Why?",
      "words": 13,
      "words_per_s": 3.18,
      "voice_over_bed_db": 15.5
    },
    {
      "id": "l02",
      "start": 4.95,
      "end": 8.881,
      "text": "Many screens give off light that vibrates one way, set by a filter.",
      "words": 13,
      "words_per_s": 3.31,
      "voice_over_bed_db": 17.3
    },
    {
      "id": "l03",
      "start": 9.3,
      "end": 14.343,
      "text": "Polarized sunglasses filter one direction too, cutting glare off water and roads.",
      "words": 12,
      "words_per_s": 2.38,
      "voice_over_bed_db": 16.7
    },
    {
      "id": "l04",
      "start": 14.8,
      "end": 18.76,
      "text": "When the filters cross, the light is blocked; turn the phone, and it passes.",
      "words": 14,
      "words_per_s": 3.54,
      "voice_over_bed_db": 16.8
    },
    {
      "id": "l05",
      "start": 19.2,
      "end": 23.855,
      "text": "So just rotate the phone. And if it darkens, your sunglasses are polarized.",
      "words": 13,
      "words_per_s": 2.79,
      "voice_over_bed_db": 16.5
    },
    {
      "id": "l06",
      "start": 26.35,
      "end": 29.639,
      "text": "Download Recall for learning any new subject with AI.",
      "words": 9,
      "words_per_s": 2.74,
      "voice_over_bed_db": 16.7
    }
  ],
